    },
    "long_instructions": "In the last level, you carefully analyzed an AI program's output and identified its shortcomings in `index.html`. Now it's time to put on your designer hat and propose solutions!\r\n\r\nYour task is to brainstorm and write down concrete improvements that would make this AI program more user-friendly, fair, and robust. Think about how you could address the issues you found, such as inaccurate classifications, unhelpful suggestions, or potential negative impacts.\r\n\r\nOpen `index.html` again. Continue adding to the HTML comments within the `<div class=\"analysis-section\">` to propose your improvements. Consider:\r\n\r\n*   **More User Input:** What additional questions could the AI ask to better understand the user's mood or preference?\r\n*   **Conditional Logic:** How could the program use rules (like \"IF mood is Sad AND user wants to chill, THEN suggest a calm song, NOT a hyper one\") to provide better recommendations?\r\n*   **User Feedback:** Could the program allow users to say \"not helpful\" and provide an alternative?\r\n*   **Options and Disclaimers:** Instead of one suggestion, could it offer a few? Could it include a message like \"This is just a suggestion, your feelings are valid\"?\r\n\r\nWrite your proposed improvements clearly in `index.html`. Be specific about what changes you would make to the AI's logic or user interaction.",
    "generate_outline": "Based on the shortcomings identified in the previous level, students will brainstorm and propose concrete improvements to make the AI program more user-friendly, fair, or robust. This could involve adding disclaimers, user feedback mechanisms, or simple conditional logic to handle edge cases."
  },
